WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:02.169
Alright everybody you know the drill.

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:05.500
We all know how we're voting but let's get
those sound bites for our donor emails.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.020
What are going to be the ground rules today?

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.120
Bring politics.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.900
I am upset about the process.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.000
We haven't even started!

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.120
Are we going to be allowed to interrupt each
other?

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:20.920
Yes!

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.620
Knock knock.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.240
Who's there?

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.080
Interrupting protester.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.040
Interrupting protester, wh-

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.980
[Unintelligible Shrieking]

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.360
That reveals the whole joke.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.780
It doesn't pass the giggle test.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.580
Okay, okay, focus people, focus!

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.040
We are here to talk about a single person.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:35.680
Hillary Clinton

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.340
Merrick Garland

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.300
Justice Kagan

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.280
Justice Sotomayor

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.380
Reverend Al Sharpton

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.180
Bill Burke

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.160
Lin-Manuel Miranda

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.700
Judge Kavanaugh

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.280
Hi!

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.320
What a bastard Donald Trump is?

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.840
We can drink in here, right?

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.700
I think the penalties are being ousted from
the Senate.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.620
I openly invite and accept the consequences.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.760
I feel like I'm a prop.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.180
Am I a prop for your thing?

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.540
Have you not seen one of these before?

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.680
It's mostly a sham.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.740
We know that every Democratic member of this
committee is going to vote no.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.560
Did you guts want to hear about my judicial
opinions?

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.680
I have over 300.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.940
Put them in a box marked 'irrelevant' and
set it aside.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:08.820
They're full of junk.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.440
These confirmation hearings haven't worked
for 31 years in America.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.680
In fairness, Congress hasn't worked for 31
years either, so...

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.180
Damn!

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.200
I'm sorry, that was harsh.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.460
Can we redact that? can we slip that under
the thousands of documents we don't talk about?

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.340
Anybody running for president over there?

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.580
How much of this hearing is just presidential
campaign fodder.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.070
10 to 15 percent.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.480
Or 50 percent or 40 percent.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.620
99 percent.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.320
100 percent.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.140
Well we got the room for three more days,
should we watch a movie?

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.560
We've never had a request for a video.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.180
Forrest Gump

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.120
Alice in Wonderland

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.580
We've seen this movie before.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.500
I hear Dinesh D'Souza has a new comedy.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.060
We need Schoolhouse Rock back.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.680
Okay, I appreciate Schoolhouse Rock, but we're
not children, we're Senators.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.240
We all understand the concept of object permanence.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.940
Don't do that, what's being hidden?

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.220
What is being hidden?

00:01:59.220 --> 00:01:59.960
Alright.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.920
Hope and pray that I will but today-

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.220
That is clearly not reflective of current
reality.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.700
That was before judges were viewed as policy
makers.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.260
There's no verse of Schoolhouse Rock that
says

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:14.180
'give a whole bunch of power to the alphabet
soup agencies

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:17.760
and let them decide what the government's
decision should be for the people.'

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.320
Because the people don't have any way to fire
the bureaucrats.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.400
Because people can't navigate their way through
the bureaucracy

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.820
they turn tot he Supreme Court looking for
politics.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.920
God help me you are making sense, are you
sure you're in the right room?

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.660
The Supreme Court becomes our substitute political
battleground.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:33.920
It's gotten really bad.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.720
You know there's been 113 justices confirmed
to the Supreme Court, right?

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.360
The first 66 were confirmed without even holding
a hearing.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.540
Not one Senator voted against Justice Scalia's
confirmation.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.260
Wait, Scalia?

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.880
Our democracy is on trial.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:48.960
Guilty!

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.440
How much more beer should we get?

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.840
Thousands of additional cases.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.700
Good call, God I'm going to miss you.

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:57.870
The question we are being asked to address
in this hearing among others

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:04.140
is whether this judge at this time in our
history will administer the law with equal justice.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.180
The indignity of equal treatment.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.280
Regardless of if they live in a poor neighborhood
or a rich neighborhood

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.580
or if they live in a small house or the White
House.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.260
What about a little pink house?

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.400
Eminent Domain, Google it.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.240
Most of my life has been spent in the courtroom.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.280
He was acquitted.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.160
He is a judge with a clear record.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:24.720
Yup!

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.300
That seems pretty clear to me.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.500
You've been accused of hating women.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.300
Not true!

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.320
Hating children.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:30.960
Kind of.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.140
Hating clean air.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:32.640
No.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.600
Wanting dirty water.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.200
What I call a bourbon.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.060
Everyone knows that you served in the Bush
administration.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:38.580
Damn it!

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.380
I know you and your reputation for nearly
30 years.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:42.680
I don't know who you are.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.900
As you know well we went to the same law school,
we clerked in the same courthouse

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.320
in Wilmington Delaware, so-

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.180
Hambone?

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.800
Oh my God!

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.640
Hambone! oh you got super bald!

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.500
You know we've had a lot of fun today,

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.840
but the current state of politics in Washington
is no laughing matter.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.260
And neither is jurisprudence, or judicial
confirmations.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.420
The third and equal branch of government under
our Constitution is one of the most-

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.900
[Vapid Shrieking]

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:10.280
Shut up! Shut up! Just shut up!

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.080
[Shrieking Continues]

